WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.165
Week 5: Location, Condition, and Existence. locate a place describe a temporary condition say what is available

2
00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:14.324
Cultural lens. The plaza as a physical and social center in many communities.

3
00:00:14.324 --> 00:00:26.417
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:38.211
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:47.253
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:47.253 --> 00:01:17.031
Model language. La plaza es el centro de la comunidad. — The square is the center of the community. La gente se reúne alrededor de la fuente. — People gather around the fountain. Caminamos por el espacio público cada tarde. — We walk through the public space every afternoon. Este lugar tiene mucha vida social. — This place has a lot of social life. No todas las plazas cumplen la misma función. — Not every square serves the same function.

7
00:01:17.031 --> 00:01:26.929
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
